  "description": "The Process 134 CR is a carbon trail mountain bike with 140mm of front travel and 134mm in the rear, built for riders who refuse to let suspension numbers dictate the day. Its carbon frame and dialled geometry keep it quick under power and sharp through corners, with enough stability and support to charge technical descents, jump lines, and everything between them. Fox suspension handles the rough stuff, while a dependable drivetrain and DT Swiss 350 hubs keep the ride crisp, reliable, and ready to disappear deep into the trail network. Pedal it farther. Push it harder. Race it, jump it, or spend the whole day looking for its limits. Call it a hard charging chameleon. It blends into nothing.",
